# Append-only project logs and docs.
#
# Every branch appends to the tail of these five files, so without a merge
# strategy they would conflict on literally every merge. `union` is a git
# built-in (no driver to install): both sides' added lines survive, in some
# order, with no conflict marker.
#
# The trade-off is that union NEVER conflicts, so it never asks — two branches
# editing the same region can leave a duplicated or oddly ordered entry. The
# senior-engineer agent tidies the merged tail as part of the merge commit,
# since it is the only actor that sees both sides.
EXECUTIONS.md  merge=union
LEARNINGS.md   merge=union
INTERFACE.md   merge=union
AGENTS.md      merge=union
FOLLOWUPS.md   merge=union

# package-lock.json is deliberately left on the default strategy: on conflict
# the fix is regeneration, not a textual merge.
#   git checkout --ours package-lock.json && npm install
